@title Clickstream data platform
@subtitle Data Engineering, Harbor Media
@date 2026-09-30

## Overview

We collect about 1800 million events per day from our apps. Those events land in a lake that analysts query.

## Architecture diagram

diagram clicks dir=LR title="Clickstream platform"

clicks: apps "Web and Mobile Apps" ext
clicks: stream "Clickstream Stream" queue "Kinesis"
clicks: fh "Firehose" stream
clicks: raw "Raw Bucket" store
clicks: cur "Curated Bucket" store
clicks: glue "Glue Catalog" store
clicks: emr "EMR Cluster" svc
clicks: rs "Redshift Cluster" db
clicks: looker "Looker" ext
clicks: group ingest "Ingest account" stream, fh
clicks: group lake "Lake VPC (10.40.0.0/16)" emr, rs
clicks: group analytics "Analytics account" raw, cur, glue, lake
clicks: apps -> stream : events
clicks: stream -> fh : batch
clicks: fh -> raw : parquet every 5 min
clicks: raw -> emr : nightly ETL
clicks: emr -> cur : cleaned tables
clicks: cur -> rs : COPY
clicks: glue -> emr : schemas
clicks: rs -> looker : SQL

## Datasets

table = Dataset,Daily volume (GB),Retention (days),Owner; raw_events,940,30,Ingest squad; sessions,120,400,Analytics Eng; page_views,310,400,Analytics Eng; ad_impressions,260,90,Ad Tech

## Known limits

- Firehose buffering means data arrives up to 5 minutes late.
- The nightly ETL finishes around 03:40 UTC.
- Redshift is a 4-node ra3.4xlarge cluster that queues queries above 50 concurrent users.
